# 012-vm-byte-at-off-by-one
#
# The encoded VM's `byteAt` admits an offset equal to the string's byte
# length and reads the padding byte past the end, where the interpreter
# and the native tier refuse. Wrong only on that offset, in encoded code.
#
# An artificial defect for measuring the fuzzing harness (issue 681).
# Never applied to this tree: scripts/fuzz-mutant.sh applies it in a
# scratch worktree. docs/FUZZ_EVALUATION.md records what found it.
diff --git a/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec/encoded.rs b/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec/encoded.rs
